  "verbalization": "Perindopril, an angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitor, is associated with Hypertensive Disorder through an off-label use pathway that links it to Diabetic Nephropathy, a condition that in turn is indicated for Captopril, Irbesartan, and Losartan. These medications are commonly used to treat hypertension, and the evidence suggests that Perindopril may be repurposed for this indication through indirect pathways. The shared mechanism of action—targeting the renin-angiotensin system—underlies the relationship between Perindopril and Hypertensive Disorder, even though the direct therapeutic relationship is not explicitly stated. The evidence is consistent across multiple off-label use links, reinforcing the hypothesis that Perindopril may be considered for hypertension treatment in certain contexts. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for repurposing Perindopril in clinical practice, particularly in patients with diabetes and hypertension.",
